From 455a0eccde7dd910d7ac3a9f22914e191e2ffe32 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 20:34:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] network: resolve an uplink's names through the uplink

A request pinned to an uplink still has its hostname resolved by the
system resolver over the default route, so content delivery networks
pick an edge for the wrong uplink. Link uplinkdns when it is found and
register each addon uplink with it, so that lookups for a socket bound
to an uplink run through that uplink, against the servers named in the
specification ("<uplink>;dns=<servers>", or a dns attribute next to
localaddress in advancedsettings.xml). A Python destination uplinkdns
stands in for is judged by its name, and CDNSNameCache asks the system
resolver, because its callers need real addresses.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
---
